Anyway, though, if you make a beeline for
Sokoban first, which tends to be a good
approach for novice players, you'll probably
be XL7 just about the time you finish up
Sokoban.  Delphi is then conveniently nearby
and on the way to the Mines, which is probably
where you'll want to go next.  Leastwise, that
has been my experience thus far.

The reason I recommend dipping at Delphi
is because there are always four fountains
on the same level there.  Thus, if you dry
up a fountain or two, you don't have to make
a long trip with a very rusty weapon before
trying again elsewhere.  It is *possible* to
dry up all four Delphi fountains and still not
have Excalibur, but it is rather unlikely.  If
you happen to find another place with at
least three fountains on the same level,
before you find Delphi, and you are of a
sufficiently high level, you could go ahead
and dip your sword (as soon as you clear
the level of its initial load of baddies).


